rules:
- id: rule-workflow-execution-model-compliance
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Workflows must adhere to the CAS execution model, separating orchestration
    responsibilities for the Runner from reasoning responsibilities for the Workflow,
    while avoiding direct repository scanning.
  title: Workflow Execution Model Compliance
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-pattern-decision-lifecycle-alignment
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Maintains clear distinction between pattern maturity (knowledge evolution)
    and decision status (governance lifecycle) to prevent premature architectural
    promotion.
  title: Pattern and Decision Lifecycle Alignment
- id: rule-patterns-born-as-supporting
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: All new patterns must be initialized with a 'supporting' scope to ensure
    validation through usage before any potential promotion to core.
  title: Patterns Must Be Created as Supporting
- id: rule-do-not-merge-across-architectural-layers
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Prevents merging or consolidation of patterns across distinct architectural
    layers to maintain separation between governance, execution, and reliability concerns.
  title: Do Not Merge Across Architectural Layers
- id: rule-promotion-requires-evidence
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Mandates that pattern promotion to the core architecture must be supported
    by strong evidence from multiple system sources or project implementations.
  title: Promotion Requires Evidence
- id: rule-architecture-work-authority
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Architecture Work items are the authoritative source for architectural
    planning state; generated artifacts must derive planning status from these items.
  title: Architecture Work Authority
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-decision-schema-must-be-structured
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Enforces the use of a structured YAML decision schema for all ADRs to enable
    machine processing and consistent system interpretation.
  title: Decision Schema Must Be Structured
- id: rule-shared-knowledge-workspace
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Projects must participate in a shared Knowledge Workspace and avoid duplicating
    global structures like runtime or template directories.
  title: Shared Knowledge Workspace
- id: rule-language-semantic-contract
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Establishes a foundational semantic contract distinguishing between intent
    (AID), state (AEM), and architect decisions (ADR) to ensure system clarity.
  title: Language & Semantics Contract
- id: rule-heuristic-patterns-require-signals
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Ensures traceability by requiring all heuristic-derived patterns to include
    at least one linked signal as foundational evidence.
  title: Heuristic-Derived Patterns Require Signals
- id: rule-precedence-hierarchy
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Defines the resolution order for rule conflicts where Global Rules take
    absolute precedence over Project and Prompt-level rules.
  title: Rule Precedence Hierarchy
- id: rule-system-proposes-architect-decides
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Maintains human-in-the-loop control by requiring all system-proposed architectural
    decisions to be explicitly accepted or rejected by an architect.
  title: System Proposes, Architect Decides
- id: rule-generated-artifacts-not-authoritative
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Generated governance artifacts act as summaries of durable source records
    and must not be treated as authoritative sources themselves.
  title: Generated Artifacts Not Authoritative
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-adr-single-source-of-truth
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Designates Architecture Decision Records (ADR) as the exclusive source
    of truth for decisions; all other representations must be derived from them.
  title: ADR as Single Source of Truth
- id: rule-signal-promotion-criteria
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Sets mandatory criteria for signal-to-pattern promotion, including recurrence
    across multiple runs, system impact, and reusability.
  title: Signal Promotion Criteria
- id: rule-decisions-must-be-persisted
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Requires all architectural decisions to be persisted as structured ADRs
    before being reflected in mapping or intent artifacts.
  title: Decisions Must Be Persisted
- id: rule-decision-status-drives-stage
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: The lifecycle stage of any architecture item must be derived from its decision
    status; items not marked 'accepted' cannot be marked as 'DONE'.
  title: Decision Status Drives Stage
- id: rule-aem-consistency-with-decisions
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: The Architecture Evolution Map must remain consistent with and never contradict
    the decisions recorded in ADRs.
  title: AEM Consistency with Decisions
- id: rule-core-patterns-must-be-foundational
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Limits core pattern classification to foundational architectural primitives
    rather than context-specific strategies or implementations.
  title: Core Patterns Must Be Foundational
summary:
  global_rules: 19
  project_rules: 0
  total_rules: 19
